# One line ending in the working tree, on every machine.
#
# git stores LF and Windows checks out CRLF by default, which is invisible until
# something READS a source file as text - and the guard tests do exactly that:
# DocumentationTests splits on "\n" and would report every library file as
# undocumented at line 1.
#
# eol=lf rather than a per-extension list: the shell scripts need LF to run at
# all, the Swift, Markdown and JSON files are all read as text by something
# here, and a rule that names extensions is a rule somebody has to remember to
# extend.
* text=auto eol=lf
